&lt;h2&gt;Margin notes&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;MathML has rendered natively in Chromium since version 109&lt;label for=&quot;sn-1&quot; class=&quot;margin-toggle sidenote-number&quot;&gt;&lt;/label&gt;&lt;input type=&quot;checkbox&quot; id=&quot;sn-1&quot; class=&quot;margin-toggle&quot;/&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;sidenote&quot;&gt;Chrome 109 shipped in January 2023, which is when MathML Core became usable in the majority browser.&lt;/span&gt;, and reached Baseline &quot;widely available&quot; in July 2025&lt;label for=&quot;sn-2&quot; class=&quot;margin-toggle sidenote-number&quot;&gt;&lt;/label&gt;&lt;input type=&quot;checkbox&quot; id=&quot;sn-2&quot; class=&quot;margin-toggle&quot;/&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;sidenote&quot;&gt;Baseline status means every current version of the major browsers supports the feature.&lt;/span&gt;. That is what makes the no-JavaScript approach viable rather than merely aspirational.&lt;/p&gt;
